 "intro": "Formal ways to concede a point, however much, and the doubled subjunctive of whatever happens.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "por más que",
   "significado": "however much",
   "pron": "por MAS ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It goes with a verb: «por más que lo intento». A real fact takes the indicative.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "por mucho que",
   "significado": "however much",
   "pron": "por MU-cho ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It goes with a verb: «por mucho que insistas». With something future or doubtful it takes the subjunctive.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "por muy",
   "significado": "however (+ adjective)",
   "pron": "por mwi",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It always takes an adjective or adverb and then «que»: «por muy tarde que sea».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "pese a",
   "significado": "despite (formal)",
   "pron": "PE-se a",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "preposition",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It takes a noun or an infinitive: «pese a la lluvia». With a conjugated verb: «pese a que».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "si bien",
   "significado": "although (formal)",
   "pron": "si BYEN",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is formal and hardly heard in speech. It is always written as two words.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "aun cuando",
   "significado": "even when, even if",
   "pron": "aun KWAN-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Here «aun» has no accent: it means «even». With an accent, «aún» means «still».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "no obstante",
   "significado": "nevertheless (formal)",
   "pron": "no obs-TAN-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is formal. It opens a new sentence and takes a comma: «No obstante, voy a seguir».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "con todo",
   "significado": "all the same",
   "pron": "kon TO-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It goes at the start of a sentence, with a comma: «Con todo, me alegro». It is like «aun así».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "digan lo que digan",
   "significado": "whatever they say",
   "pron": "DI-gan lo ke DI-gan",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It repeats the verb in the subjunctive: «digan lo que digan». It is «whatever they may say».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "pase lo que pase",
   "significado": "whatever happens",
   "pron": "PA-se lo ke PA-se",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The same verb twice, both in the subjunctive. It suits promises: «pase lo que pase, iré».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "quieras o no",
